<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pietro Verri</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1728–1797</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pietro Verri was a Milanese economist, historian and writer and a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-enlightenment">Italian Enlightenment</a>. With his brother Alessandro he formed the Accademia dei Pugni and its journal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/il-caffe">Il Caffè</a> (1764–1766), and he encouraged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-beccaria">Cesare Beccaria</a>'s work on penal reform. He served in the Austrian administration of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> and wrote Meditations on Political Economy (1771) and a history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pietro-verri.jpg" alt="Pietro Verri" width="320" height="577" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nansfeld · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pietro_Verri.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
